lor names to RGB triplets.\n* **Layout & Data Structures (`rich.layout`, `rich.table`, `rich.panel`, `rich._ratio`)**:\n  - High-level containers (`Table`, `Panel`, `Columns`, `Tree`, `Layout`).\n  - `rich._ratio` provides mathematical solvers (`ratio_distribute`, `ratio_resolve`) for dividing available terminal cells among flexible and fixed-width components.\n* **Text & Markup (`rich.text`, `rich.markup`, `rich.highlighter`)**:\n  - `Text` manages character spans and styling offsets.\n  - `rich.markup` parses BBCode-like terminal markup (e.g., `[bold red]Alert[/]`).\n\n---\n\n## 2. Engineering Standards & Conventions\n\n1. **Strict Type Annotations**:\n   - Every function, method parameter, and return type must have explicit Python type annotations (`typing`).\n   - Code must satisfy `mypy` without errors.\n2. **Pure Python & Zero Dependency Invariant**:\n   - Never introduce external third-party dependencies.\n   - Maintain compatibility across supported Python versions (3.8+).\n3. **Immutability & Stateless Rendering**:\n   - Do not mutate passed `ConsoleOptions` instances; use `options.update(...)` to derive child constraints.\n   - Never write directly to private console buffers (`console._buffer`). Always yield `Segment` instances.\n4. **Code Formatting**:\n   - Code adheres to standard `black` formatting and strict docstring conventions.\n\n---\n\n## 3. Testing & Verification Workflow\n\n`pytest` and all Rich dependencies are pre-installed in the environment. Always verify your changes using targeted `pytest` commands for the relevant module(s) before concluding your turn:\n\n```bash\n# Run ratio and table layout tests\npytest tests/test_ratio.py tests/test_table.py -q\n\n# Run styling and markup tests\npytest tests/test_style.py tests/test_markup.py -q\n\n# Run protocol and container tests\npytest tests/test_protocol.py tests/test_panel.py -q\n```\n\n---\n\n## 4. Architectural Knowledge Base (`ki-manager` MCP)\n\nThis repository is indexed by [**`ki-manager`**](https://github.com/Laeryid/KI-base), an active MCP server exposing curated Knowledge Items (KIs) and Architecture Decision Records (ADRs) with exact file locations, line ranges, and architectural invariants.\n\n### Available MCP Tools (Direct Exposure)\n- `mcp__ki_manager__ki_search`: BM25 search across all KIs and ADRs (`query`, `scope=\"all\"|\"ki\"|\"adr\"`, `limit`).\n- `mcp__ki_manager__ki_read`: Read a specific KI or ADR by filename (`rel_path`, optional `section`).\n- `mcp__ki_manager__ki_list`: List all registered KIs and ADRs (`scope=\"all\"|\"ki\"|\"adr\"`).\n- `mcp__ki_manager__ki_instructions`: Retrieve workflow instructions (`document=\"overview\"|\"knowledge-items\"`).\n\n### Mandatory Agent Workflow\n1. **Query `ki-manager` FIRST (Before Reading Source Code)**:\n   - Always start your task by calling `mcp__ki_manager__ki_search(query=\"...\")` or `mcp__ki_manager__ki_read(rel_path=\"...\")` for the relevant KI and ADR from the tables below.\n   - The Knowledge Items contain **exact line numbers and method invariants** (e.g. `L523–L585` in `rich/table.py` or `L2342–L2415` in `rich/console.py`).\n2. **Use Targeted File Reads (`offset` / `limit`)**:\n   - Once `mcp__ki_manager__ki_read` gives you the exact line numbers and invariants, use `read(path=\"...\", offset=..., limit=...)` to inspect only the target lines instead of reading entire 1,000–2,600 line files.\n   - Always ensure your changes strictly comply with the relevant ADRs (`0001`–`0004`).\n\n### Knowledge Items Manifest\n\n| File | Topic / Summary |\n| :--- | :--- |\n| `KI_rich_align.md` | Central pipeline of Rich: houses the primary `Console` class, ANSI escape sequence decoder, cell width calculators, border box constants, and alignment/column containers. It coordinates measurement, rendering, and terminal stream emission. |\n| `KI_rich_default.md` | Houses split-screen terminal layout panes (`Layout`), pattern regex highlighters (`Highlighter`), JSON syntax formatters, Rich logging handlers (`RichHandler`), default theme color rules, and Jupyter notebook rendering shims. |\n| `KI_rich_emoji.md` | Provides core emoji parsing, color representation (RGB/triplets/ANSI palettes), Windows console detection/rendering, and library top-level entry points. It translates high-level text embellishments and color palettes into terminal-safe output. |\n| `KI_rich_live.md` | Manages dynamic terminal updates, animations, multi-task progress bars, HTML/SVG export templates, and IPython integration. It allows real-time interactive terminal applications to refresh without screen scrolling. |\n| `KI_rich_markdown.md` | Provides markdown document parsing, console markup parsing (`[bold red]...[/]`), framed panel containers (`Panel`), recursive object pretty-printing (`Pretty`), user interactive prompts (`Prompt`), and the Rich Console Protocol definitions. |\n| `KI_rich_null.md` | Provides internal mathematical routines, layout ratio solvers, text wrapping primitives, platform Win32 console structures, and base ABC protocols. It forms the low-level foundation for rendering algorithms. |\n| `KI_rich_region.md` | Defines the atomic rendering primitives of Rich: `Segment` (minimal text+style tuple), `Style` (ANSI attributes container), `Rule` (horizontal dividing lines), `Status` (loading indicators with spinners), and alternate screen buffer controls (`Screen`). |\n| `KI_rich_syntax.md` | Implements high-level data presentation components: `Table` (grid formatting with auto-wrapping), `Text` (styled character spans), `Syntax` (Pygments code highlighting), `Traceback` (rich exception rendering), and `Tree` (hierarchical tree visualizations). |\n| `KI_rich_unicode11-0-0.md` | Contains precomputed Unicode East Asian Width lookup tables for modern Unicode specifications (versions 11.0.0 through 17.0.0, plus 4.1.0). These tables determine whether individual Unicode codepoints occupy 0, 1, or 2 terminal character cells. |\n| `KI_rich_unicode5-0-0.md` | Stores precomputed character width lookup tables for historical Unicode versions (versions 5.0.0 through 9.0.0). It provides backward-compatible East Asian Width measurements for legacy terminal environments and older OS consoles. |\n| `_OVERVIEW.ki.md` | Architectural master blueprint, layer boundaries, and core design invariants of the Rich library. |\n\n### Architecture Decision Records (ADRs)\n\n| ID | Title | Status | Date | File |\n| :---: | :--- | :---: | :---: | :--- |\n| **0001** | Terminal Segments & Atomic Decomposition | Accepted | 2026-11-08 | `.ki-base/decisions/0001-terminal-segments.md` |\n| **0002** | Render Protocol & Component Isolation | Accepted | 2026-11-08 | `.ki-base/decisions/0002-render-protocol.md` |\n| **0003** | Style Composition & ANSI Sequences | Accepted | 2026-11-08 | `.ki-base/decisions/0003-style-composition-and-ansi.md` |\n| **0004** | Ratio Distribution & Column Allocation | Accepted | 2026-11-08 | `.ki-base/decisions/0004-ratio-distribution-and-layout.md` |\n\n</project_instructions>\n</project_context>","cwd":"<cwd>\n/app\n</cwd>"},"timestamp":1794174251149,"toolsAdded":[{"name":"read","description":"Read the contents of a file. Supports text files and images (jpg, png, gif, webp, bmp). Images are sent as attachments. For text files, output is truncated to 2000 lines or 50KB (whichever is hit first). Use offset/limit for large files. When you need the full file, continue with offset until complete.","parameters":{"type":"object","required":["path"],"properties":{"path":{"type":"string","description":"Path to the file to read (relative or absolute)"},"offset":{"type":"number","description":"Line number to start reading from (1-indexed)"},"limit":{"type":"number","description":"Maximum number of lines to read"}}},"constrainedSampling":{"type":"json_schema","strict":"prefer"}},{"name":"bash","description":"Execute a bash command in the current working directory. Returns stdout and stderr. Output is truncated to last 2000 lines or 50KB (whichever is hit first). If truncated, full output is saved to a temp file. Optionally provide a timeout in seconds.","parameters":{"type":"object","required":["command"],"properties":{"command":{"type":"string","description":"Shell command to execute"},"timeout":{"type":"number","description":"Timeout in seconds (optional, no default timeout)"}}},"constrainedSampling":{"type":"json_schema","strict":"prefer"}},{"name":"edit","description":"Edit a single file using exact text replacement. Every edits[].oldText must match a unique, non-overlapping region of the original file. If two changes affect the same block or nearby lines, merge them into one edit instead of emitting overlapping edits. Do not include large unchanged regions just to connect distant changes.","parameters":{"type":"object","required":["path","edits"],"properties":{"path":{"type":"string","description":"Path to the file to edit (relative or absolute)"},"edits":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"object","required":["oldText","newText"],"properties":{"oldText":{"type":"string","description":"Exact text for one targeted replacement. It must be unique in the original file and must not overlap with any other edits[].oldText in the same call."},"newText":{"type":"string","description":"Replacement text for this targeted edit."}}},"description":"One or more targeted replacements. Each edit is matched against the original file, not incrementally. Do not include overlapping or nested edits. If two changes touch the same block or nearby lines, merge them into one edit instead."}}},"constrainedSampling":{"type":"json_schema","strict":"prefer"}},{"name":"write","description":"Write content to a file. Creates the file if it doesn't exist, overwrites if it does. Automatically creates parent directories.","parameters":{"type":"object","required":["path","content"],"properties":{"path":{"type":"string","description":"Path to the file to write (relative or absolute)"},"content":{"type":"string","description":"Content to write to the file"}}},"constrainedSampling":{"type":"json_schema","strict":"prefer"}},{"name":"grep","description":"Search file contents for a pattern. Returns matching lines with file paths and line numbers. Respects .gitignore. Output is truncated to 100 matches or 50KB (whichever is hit first). Long lines are truncated to 500 chars.","parameters":{"type":"object","required":["pattern"],"properties":{"pattern":{"type":"string","description":"Search pattern (regex or literal string)"},"path":{"type":"string","description":"Directory or file to search (default: current directory)"},"glob":{"type":"string","description":"Filter files by glob pattern, e.g. '*.ts' or '**/*.spec.ts'"},"ignoreCase":{"type":"boolean","description":"Case-insensitive search (default: false)"},"literal":{"type":"boolean","description":"Treat pattern as literal string instead of regex (default: false)"},"context":{"type":"number","description":"Number of lines to show before and after each match (default: 0)"},"limit":{"type":"number","description":"Maximum number of matches to return (default: 100)"}}}},{"name":"find","description":"Search for files by glob pattern. Returns matching file paths relative to the search directory. Respects .gitignore. Output is truncated to 1000 results or 50KB (whichever is hit first).","parameters":{"type":"object","required":["pattern"],"properties":{"pattern":{"type":"string","description":"Glob pattern to match files, e.g. '*.ts', '**/*.json', or 'src/**/*.spec.ts'"},"path":{"type":"string","description":"Directory to search in (default: current directory)"},"limit":{"type":"number","description":"Maximum number of results (default: 1000)"}}}},{"name":"ls","description":"List directory contents. Returns entries sorted alphabetically, with '/' suffix for directories. Includes dotfiles. Output is truncated to 500 entries or 50KB (whichever is hit first).","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"path":{"type":"string","description":"Directory to list (default: current directory)"},"limit":{"type":"number","description":"Maximum number of entries to return (default: 500)"}}}},{"name":"mcp__ki_manager__ki_instructions","description":"Get workflow instructions and project rules for ki-manager. Available documents:\n- 'overview' — global AI rules and project navigation\n- 'knowledge-items' — table of registered KI files\n- 'create-adr' — workflow: document architectural decisions\n- 'expand-knowledge' — workflow: deep enrichment of KI files\n- 'scaffold-knowledge' — workflow: bulk scaffold of uncovered modules\n- 'sync-knowledge' — workflow: sync KI after code changes\nCall this before starting any documentation workflow task.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"document":{"type":"string","description":"Document name from the list above (e.g. 'create-adr')"}},"required":["document"]}},{"name":"mcp__ki_manager__ki_list","description":"List Knowledge Items (KI) and Architecture Decision Records (ADRs) registered in the active project. Provides a structured overview of all documented modules, topics, and architectural decisions.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"scope":{"type":"string","enum":["all","ki","adr"],"default":"all","description":"Filter by document type: 'all' (default), 'ki' (Knowledge Items), or 'adr' (Architecture Decision Records)."},"format":{"type":"string","enum":["markdown","json"],"default":"markdown","description":"Output format: 'markdown' (structured tables, default) or 'json'."},"filter":{"type":"string","description":"Optional substring to filter by filename, title, summary, or covered module."}}}},{"name":"mcp__ki_manager__ki_search","description":"Search Knowledge Items (KI) and ADRs by keywords using BM25 ranking (pure Python). Returns matching paths, titles, relevance scores, and text snippets. Use this tool to find relevant documentation without full codebase scans.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"query":{"type":"string","description":"Search query keywords (e.g. 'workspace detection' or 'dependency management')."},"scope":{"type":"string","enum":["all","ki","adr"],"default":"all","description":"Scope of search: 'all' (default), 'ki' (knowledge items), or 'adr' (architecture decision records)."},"limit":{"type":"integer","default":5,"description":"Maximum number of results to return (default: 5)."},"offset":{"type":"integer","default":0,"description":"Result offset for pagination (default: 0)."},"page":{"type":"integer","minimum":1,"default":1,"description":"Page number for pagination (1-based, alternative to offset)."},"format":{"type":"string","enum":["markdown","json"],"default":"markdown","description":"Output format: 'markdown' (compact list, default) or 'json'."}},"required":["query"]}},{"name":"mcp__ki_manager__ki_read","description":"Read a Knowledge Item (KI) or ADR markdown file. Supports optional section filtering (by markdown header), character limits, and offset.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"rel_path":{"type":"string","description":"Path or filename of the Knowledge Item or ADR (e.g. 'KI_architecture.md', 'knowledge/KI_architecture.md', or '001_some.md')."},"section":{"type":"string","description":"Optional markdown section title to extract (e.g. 'Architecture' or 'Known Issues')."},"max_chars":{"type":"integer","description":"Optional maximum number of characters to return (truncates if exceeded)."},"offset":{"type":"integer","default":0,"description":"Optional character offset to start reading from (default: 0)."}},"required":["rel_path"]}},{"name":"mcp__ki_manager__ki_tools","description":"Inspect available ki-manager tools and their schemas. Call without arguments to list all tools grouped by category. Provide 'name' to inspect the exact inputSchema of a specific tool before calling it via ki_call or ki_mutate.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"name":{"type":"string","description":"Optional tool name to get full JSON schema (e.g. 'audit_coverage')."},"group":{"type":"string","description":"Optional category group filter (init_registry, coverage_analysis, scaffold, config_adr, files, git_state)."}}}},{"name":"mcp__ki_manager__ki_call","description":"Execute a read-only ki-manager tool. Available tools: analyze_all_dependencies, analyze_dependencies, analyze_module, audit_coverage, check_ki_drift, find_unmapped_files, generate_dir_index, git_diff_secured, ki_graph_visualize, ki_list_projects, ki_scaffold_status, ki_split_analyze, ki_status, read_know_file. Use ki_tools(name=...) to check arguments. For mutating operations, use ki_mutate.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"tool":{"type":"string","description":"Name of the read-only tool to call.","enum":["analyze_all_dependencies","analyze_dependencies","analyze_module","audit_coverage","check_ki_drift","find_unmapped_files","generate_dir_index","git_diff_secured","ki_graph_visualize","ki_list_projects","ki_scaffold_status","ki_split_analyze","ki_status","read_know_file"]},"args":{"type":"object","description":"Arguments dictionary to pass to the tool.","default":{}}},"required":["tool"]}},{"name":"mcp__ki_manager__ki_mutate","description":"Execute a state-modifying ki-manager tool. Available tools: add_ki_to_config, create_adr, edit_doc_config, edit_know_file, git_checkpoint, git_restore, ki_finalize_scaffolds, ki_init_project, ki_migrate_project, ki_prune_registry, ki_register_project, ki_scaffold, ki_split, make_know_dir, restore_mapping, save_state, sync_agents_md, update_last_verified, write_know_file. Use ki_tools(name=...) to check arguments.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"tool":{"type":"string","description":"Name of the mutating tool to call.","enum":["add_ki_to_config","create_adr","edit_doc_config","edit_know_file","git_checkpoint","git_restore","ki_finalize_scaffolds","ki_init_project","ki_migrate_project","ki_prune_registry","ki_register_project","ki_scaffold","ki_split","make_know_dir","restore_mapping","save_state","sync_agents_md","update_last_verified","write_know_file"]},"args":{"type":"object","description":"Arguments dictionary to pass to the tool.","default":{}}},"required":["tool"]}}]}}
{"type":"message_start","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Component Implementation: Embeddable `Badge` UI Component\n\nProblem Description:\nDevelop a new visual status badge component `Badge` in `rich/badge.py` (and export it in `rich/__init__.py` and `rich.__all__`).\nThe component must be fully compatible with Rich's layout and rendering pipeline so that it can be printed directly via `console.print(badge)` or embedded seamlessly inside Tables, Panels, Columns, and Trees.\n\nArchitectural Standard:\nThe component must strictly adhere to the internal architectural conventions of this repository (as documented in the project Architecture Decision Records). It must implement the standard streaming render protocol and measurement protocol accepted in the codebase, properly handling standalone and nested layouts without breaking composition or accessing private console state.\n\nRequirements:\n1. Create `rich/badge.py`:\n   - Class `Badge`:\n     ```python\n     def __init__(\n         self,\n         text: str,\n         *,\n         style: StyleType = \"bold white on blue\",\n         border_style: StyleType = \"blue\",\n         pill: bool = True,\n         icon: Optional[str] = None,\n     ) -> None:\n     ```\n   - When `pill=True`, formats the badge with curved pill borders `( ` ... ` )`.\n   - When `pill=False`, formats with square borders `[ ` ... ` ]`.\n   - If `icon` is provided, includes `icon + \" \" + text`.\n   - Accurately reports cell measurement based on character cell lengths.\n2. In `rich/__init__.py`:\n   - Expose `Badge` in `__all__` and make it importable from the top-level `rich` package.\n3. Verification:\n   - Must comply with project architectural standards and render cleanly when printed standalone or nested inside Tables and Panels.\n   - All existing tests must continue to pass without regressions."}],"timestamp":1794174251148}}
{"type":"message_end","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Component Implementation: Embeddable `Badge` UI Component\n\nProblem Description:\nDevelop a new visual status badge component `Badge` in `rich/badge.py` (and export it in `rich/__init__.py` and `rich.__all__`).\nThe component must be fully compatible with Rich's layout and rendering pipeline so that it can be printed directly via `console.print(badge)` or embedded seamlessly inside Tables, Panels, Columns, and Trees.\n\nArchitectural Standard:\nThe component must strictly adhere to the internal architectural conventions of this repository (as documented in the project Architecture Decision Records). It must implement the standard streaming render protocol and measurement protocol accepted in the codebase, properly handling standalone and nested layouts without breaking composition or accessing private console state.\n\nRequirements:\n1. Create `rich/badge.py`:\n   - Class `Badge`:\n     ```python\n     def __init__(\n         self,\n         text: str,\n         *,\n         style: StyleType = \"bold white on blue\",\n         border_style: StyleType = \"blue\",\n         pill: bool = True,\n         icon: Optional[str] = None,\n     ) -> None:\n     ```\n   - When `pill=True`, formats the badge with curved pill borders `( ` ... ` )`.\n   - When `pill=False`, formats with square borders `[ ` ... ` ]`.\n   - If `icon` is provided, includes `icon + \" \" + text`.\n   - Accurately reports cell measurement based on character cell lengths.\n2. In `rich/__init__.py`:\n   - Expose `Badge` in `__all__` and make it importable from the top-level `rich` package.\n3. Verification:\n   - Must comply with project architectural standards and render cleanly when printed standalone or nested inside Tables and Panels.\n   - All existing tests must continue to pass without regressions."}],"timestamp":1794174251148}}
