Global default `Console` instance accessor.\n- `rich.traceback.install()`: Installs Rich exception handler for formatted stack traces.\n\n## Testing & Verification\n\n- Test command: `pytest tests/`\n\n## Architecture Notes\n\n- Follows the Rich Console Protocol (`__rich__` and `__rich_console__`).\n- Renders to atomic `Segment` instances before emitting ANSI escape sequences or Win32 calls.\n- Supports degradation/fallbacks for terminals without 24-bit TrueColor or Windows legacy console environments.\n\n## Related KIs\n\n- [[KI_rich_align.md]]\n- [[KI_rich_region.md]]\n- [[KI_rich_syntax.md]]\n- [[KI_rich_markdown.md]]\n- [[KI_rich_default.md]]\n- [[KI_rich_live.md]]\n- [[KI_rich_emoji.md]]\n- [[KI_rich_null.md]]\n- [[KI_rich_unicode11-0-0.md]]\n- [[KI_rich_unicode5-0-0.md]]\n"}],"details":{"server":"ki-manager","tool":"ki_read"},"isError":false,"durationMs":32,"timestamp":1794174252633}}
{"type":"message_end","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"tool_mcp__ki_manager__ki_read_3qShDGOt3POXP7xmeJgs","toolName":"mcp__ki_manager__ki_read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"<!-- last_verified: 2026-11-08 -->\n# _OVERVIEW — Project Overview\n\n**Module**: `rich` (entire project)\n**Last verified**: 2026-11-08\n\n## Overview\n\nRich is a Python library for rendering rich text, tables, syntax highlighting, markdown, progress bars, and formatted data to terminal output and HTML. It serves as the primary rendering engine across console applications to provide modern CLI UX.\n\n## Subsystems & Knowledge Architecture\n\nThe codebase is partitioned into cohesive Knowledge Items (max 10 files per item):\n\n- [[KI_rich_align.md]]: Central `Console` orchestrator, ANSI escape parsing, cells width measurement, borders, and column layouts.\n- [[KI_rich_region.md]]: Low-level rendering primitives: `Segment`, `Style`, `Rule`, `Status`, `Spinner`, and screen switching.\n- [[KI_rich_syntax.md]]: Data presentation components: `Table`, `Text`, `Syntax`, `Traceback`, `Tree`, and `Theme`.\n- [[KI_rich_markdown.md]]: Markdown AST rendering, console `[markup]`, `Panel`, `Pretty` printing, and `Prompt` inputs.\n- [[KI_rich_default.md]]: Proportional multi-pane `Layout`, regex `Highlighter`, `RichHandler` logging, and JSON formatting.\n- [[KI_rich_live.md]]: Dynamic terminal updating (`Live`), multi-task progress meters (`Progress`), and IPython shims.\n- [[KI_rich_emoji.md]]: Emoji parsing, `Color` color models (Standard/256/Truecolor), and Windows console backends.\n- [[KI_rich_null.md]]: Internal ratio math, text wrapping routines, and Win32 low-level structures.\n- [[KI_rich_unicode11-0-0.md]] & [[KI_rich_unicode5-0-0.md]]: Unicode East Asian character width lookup tables.\n\n## Entry Points & Public API\n\n- `rich.print`: Direct drop-in replacement for `print()` with rich markup formatting.\n- `rich.inspect`: Introspective object visualizer.\n- `rich.get_console()`: Global default `Console` instance accessor.\n- `rich.traceback.install()`: Installs Rich exception handler for formatted stack traces.\n\n## Testing & Verification\n\n- Test command: `pytest tests/`\n\n## Architecture Notes\n\n- Follows the Rich Console Protocol (`__rich__` and `__rich_console__`).\n- Renders to atomic `Segment` instances before emitting ANSI escape sequences or Win32 calls.\n- Supports degradation/fallbacks for terminals without 24-bit TrueColor or Windows legacy console environments.\n\n## Related KIs\n\n- [[KI_rich_align.md]]\n- [[KI_rich_region.md]]\n- [[KI_rich_syntax.md]]\n- [[KI_rich_markdown.md]]\n- [[KI_rich_default.md]]\n- [[KI_rich_live.md]]\n- [[KI_rich_emoji.md]]\n- [[KI_rich_null.md]]\n- [[KI_rich_unicode11-0-0.md]]\n- [[KI_rich_unicode5-0-0.md]]\n"}],"details":{"server":"ki-manager","tool":"ki_read"},"isError":false,"durationMs":32,"timestamp":1794174252633}}
{"type":"message_start","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"tool_mcp__ki_manager__ki_read_FPa63nxXzUqGl5Txe3Xu","toolName":"mcp__ki_manager__ki_read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# ADR-0002: Render Protocol & Component Isolation\n\n- **Status:** Accepted\n- **Date:** 2026-11-08\n- **Deciders:** Rich Architectural Maintainers\n\n## Context\n\nRich supports arbitrary nested UI components (such as Panels inside Tables inside Trees). If custom components were allowed to mutate shared rendering options or directly manipulate the `Console` buffer, rendering would become non-deterministic, thread-unsafe, and incompatible with real-time displays like `Live` and `Progress`.\n\n## Decision\n\n1. **Mandatory Console Protocol:**  \n   All visual components must implement the public generator protocol:\n   ```python\n   def __rich_console__(self, console: \"Console\", options: \"ConsoleOptions\") -> \"RenderResult\":\n       ...\n       yield Segment(...)\n   ```\n   A component may optionally implement `__rich_measure__(self, console: \"Console\", options: \"ConsoleOptions\") -> Measurement` for dynamic sizing.\n\n2. **Strict Component Isolation Invariants:**\n   - **No Buffer Access:** Components must NEVER access or write to `console._buffer` or `console.file` directly. All output must be returned via `yield` as an iterable of `Segment` or renderable objects.\n   - **Options Immutability:** The passed `options: ConsoleOptions` instance is strictly read-only. Components must never mutate its fields. To adjust constraints for child components, use `options.update(...)` which returns a fresh copy.\n   - **Stateless Yielding:** Generators must be re-entrant and idempotent so that multiple render passes (e.g. measuring then rendering) produce identical results without side effects.\n\n3. **Internal Spacing Convention for Inline Badges:**\n   - In accordance with repository design conventions, inline badge components must enclose their inner text with exactly one space of padding inside the boundary caps: `\"( \"` + content + `\" )\"` for pill badges, and `\"[\" + \" \"` + content + `\" ]\"` for square badges.\n   - Example: `Badge(\"DEPLOYED\", pill=True, icon=\"★\")` must yield segments rendering as `\"( ★ DEPLOYED )\"`. Square badges render as `\"[ SYSTEM ALERT ]\"`. Measurement must include the 4 cells occupied by borders and inner spaces.\n\n## Consequences\n\n- Components can be composed arbitrarily without side effects.\n- Direct console buffer writes or mutating shared options is treated as an architectural violation and rejected in code review.\n- Ensures seamless integration with `Live` displays and virtual screen buffers.\n"}],"details":{"server":"ki-manager","tool":"ki_read"},"isError":false,"durationMs":44,"timestamp":1794174252636}}
{"type":"message_end","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"tool_mcp__ki_manager__ki_read_FPa63nxXzUqGl5Txe3Xu","toolName":"mcp__ki_manager__ki_read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# ADR-0002: Render Protocol & Component Isolation\n\n- **Status:** Accepted\n- **Date:** 2026-11-08\n- **Deciders:** Rich Architectural Maintainers\n\n## Context\n\nRich supports arbitrary nested UI components (such as Panels inside Tables inside Trees). If custom components were allowed to mutate shared rendering options or directly manipulate the `Console` buffer, rendering would become non-deterministic, thread-unsafe, and incompatible with real-time displays like `Live` and `Progress`.\n\n## Decision\n\n1. **Mandatory Console Protocol:**  \n   All visual components must implement the public generator protocol:\n   ```python\n   def __rich_console__(self, console: \"Console\", options: \"ConsoleOptions\") -> \"RenderResult\":\n       ...\n       yield Segment(...)\n   ```\n   A component may optionally implement `__rich_measure__(self, console: \"Console\", options: \"ConsoleOptions\") -> Measurement` for dynamic sizing.\n\n2. **Strict Component Isolation Invariants:**\n   - **No Buffer Access:** Components must NEVER access or write to `console._buffer` or `console.file` directly. All output must be returned via `yield` as an iterable of `Segment` or renderable objects.\n   - **Options Immutability:** The passed `options: ConsoleOptions` instance is strictly read-only. Components must never mutate its fields. To adjust constraints for child components, use `options.update(...)` which returns a fresh copy.\n   - **Stateless Yielding:** Generators must be re-entrant and idempotent so that multiple render passes (e.g. measuring then rendering) produce identical results without side effects.\n\n3. **Internal Spacing Convention for Inline Badges:**\n   - In accordance with repository design conventions, inline badge components must enclose their inner text with exactly one space of padding inside the boundary caps: `\"( \"` + content + `\" )\"` for pill badges, and `\"[\" + \" \"` + content + `\" ]\"` for square badges.\n   - Example: `Badge(\"DEPLOYED\", pill=True, icon=\"★\")` must yield segments rendering as `\"( ★ DEPLOYED )\"`. Square badges render as `\"[ SYSTEM ALERT ]\"`. Measurement must include the 4 cells occupied by borders and inner spaces.\n\n## Consequences\n\n- Components can be composed arbitrarily without side effects.\n- Direct console buffer writes or mutating shared options is treated as an architectural violation and rejected in code review.\n- Ensures seamless integration with `Live` displays and virtual screen buffers.\n"}],"details":{"server":"ki-manager","tool":"ki_read"},"isError":false,"durationMs":44,"timestamp":1794174252636}}
{"type":"message_start","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"tool_mcp__ki_manager__ki_read_uhx8UJ6Q0Gs1Bn5mu9H3","toolName":"mcp__ki_manager__ki_read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# ADR-0003: Style Composition & ANSI Sequences\n\n- **Status:** Accepted\n- **Date:** 2026-11-08\n- **Deciders:** Rich Architectural Maintainers\n\n## Context\n\nStyling in terminals requires combining foreground colors, background colors, links, and various text attributes (bold, italic, underline, reverse, etc.). Rich needs an immutable, high-performance styling algebra that supports cascading inheritance, markup parsing, and export to both ANSI terminals and web formats (HTML/SVG).\n\n## Decision\n\n1. **Immutable Style Class:**  \n   The `Style` object is immutable and hashable with internal caching:\n   - Attributes (bold, underline, double_underline, italic, blink, etc.) use tri-state values (`True`, `False`, `None` where `None` indicates inherit/unset).\n2. **Style Composition Algebra (`+` operator):**  \n   Style addition (`style1 + style2`) cascades attributes from left to right:\n   - Attributes defined in `style2` override attributes in `style1` if set (`is not None`).\n   - Unset attributes (`None`) in `style2` inherit values from `style1`.\n3. **ANSI Sequence Mapping & Exporters:**  \n   Every new style modifier must maintain synchronization across:\n   - Terminal ANSI code generator: open code (e.g. `\\x1b[4:2m` or `\\x1b[21m`) and reset/close code.\n   - Default style definitions (`rich/default_styles.py`).\n   - Markup parser (`rich/markup.py`) to recognize `[modifier]...[/]`.\n   - Exporters (`rich/terminal_theme.py`, `rich/_export_format.py`) for SVG and HTML rendering.\n\n## Consequences\n\n- Full consistency between CLI console output, HTML export, and SVG snapshots.\n- Guarantees predictable cascading style resolution across nested tags.\n"}],"details":{"server":"ki-manager","tool":"ki_read"},"isError":false,"durationMs":56,"timestamp":1794174252646}}
{"type":"message_end","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"tool_mcp__ki_manager__ki_read_uhx8UJ6Q0Gs1Bn5mu9H3","toolName":"mcp__ki_manager__ki_read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# ADR-0003: Style Composition & ANSI Sequences\n\n- **Status:** Accepted\n- **Date:** 2026-11-08\n- **Deciders:** Rich Architectural Maintainers\n\n## Context\n\nStyling in terminals requires combining foreground colors, background colors, links, and various text attributes (bold, italic, underline, reverse, etc.). Rich needs an immutable, high-performance styling algebra that supports cascading inheritance, markup parsing, and export to both ANSI terminals and web formats (HTML/SVG).\n\n## Decision\n\n1. **Immutable Style Class:**  \n   The `Style` object is immutable and hashable with internal caching:\n   - Attributes (bold, underline, double_underline, italic, blink, etc.) use tri-state values (`True`, `False`, `None` where `None` indicates inherit/unset).\n2. **Style Composition Algebra (`+` operator):**  \n   Style addition (`style1 + style2`) cascades attributes from left to right:\n   - Attributes defined in `style2` override attributes in `style1` if set (`is not None`).\n   - Unset attributes (`None`) in `style2` inherit values from `style1`.\n3. **ANSI Sequence Mapping & Exporters:**  \n   Every new style modifier must maintain synchronization across:\n   - Terminal ANSI code generator: open code (e.g. `\\x1b[4:2m` or `\\x1b[21m`) and reset/close code.\n   - Default style definitions (`rich/default_styles.py`).\n   - Markup parser (`rich/markup.py`) to recognize `[modifier]...[/]`.\n   - Exporters (`rich/terminal_theme.py`, `rich/_export_format.py`) for SVG and HTML rendering.\n\n## Consequences\n\n- Full consistency between CLI console output, HTML export, and SVG snapshots.\n- Guarantees predictable cascading style resolution across nested tags.\n"}],"details":{"server":"ki-manager","tool":"ki_read"},"isError":false,"durationMs":56,"timestamp":1794174252646}}
{"type":"turn_end","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I will start by reviewing the architectural overview of the `rich` library and the ADRs related to the render protocol and style composition, to ensure that the new `Badge` component adheres to the project's standards."},{"type":"toolCall","id":"tool_mcp__ki_manager__ki_read_3qShDGOt3POXP7xmeJgs","name":"mcp__ki_manager__ki_read","arguments":{"rel_path":"_OVERVIEW.ki.md"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"tool_mcp__ki_manager__ki_read_FPa63nxXzUqGl5Txe3Xu","name":"mcp__ki_manager__ki_read","arguments":{"rel_path":".ki-base/decisions/0002-render-protocol.md"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"tool_mcp__ki_manager__ki_read_uhx8UJ6Q0Gs1Bn5mu9H3","name":"mcp__ki_manager__ki_read","arguments":{"rel_path":".ki-base/decisions/0003-style-composition-and-ansi.md"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"openrouter","model":"google/gemini-2.5-flash","usage":{"input":5871,"output":157,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":0,"totalTokens":6028,"cost":{"input":0.0017613,"output":0.00039250000000000005,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.0021538,"totalFromProvider":true}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1794174251175,"responseId":"gen-1794174251-MX5xJ9JdGZ6h0lAJdmDq","rawStopReason":"tool_calls","durationMs":1394,"thinkingLevel":"off"},"toolResults":[{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"tool_mcp__ki_manager__ki_read_3qShDGOt3POXP7xmeJgs","toolName":"mcp__ki_manager__ki_read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"<!-- last_verified: 2026-11-08 -->\n# _OVERVIEW — Project Overview\n\n**Module**: `rich` (entire project)\n**Last verified**: 2026-11-08\n\n## Overview\n\nRich is a Python library for rendering rich text, tables, syntax highlighting, markdown, progress bars, and formatted data to terminal output and HTML. It serves as the primary rendering engine across console applications to provide modern CLI UX.\n\n## Subsystems & Knowledge Architecture\n\nThe codebase is partitioned into cohesive Knowledge Items (max 10 files per item):\n\n- [[KI_rich_align.md]]: Central `Console` orchestrator, ANSI escape parsing, cells width measurement, borders, and column layouts.\n- [[KI_rich_region.md]]: Low-level rendering primitives: `Segment`, `Style`, `Rule`, `Status`, `Spinner`, and screen switching.\n- [[KI_rich_syntax.md]]: Data presentation components: `Table`, `Text`, `Syntax`, `Traceback`, `Tree`, and `Theme`.\n- [[KI_rich_markdown.md]]: Markdown AST rendering, console `[markup]`, `Panel`, `Pretty` printing, and `Prompt` inputs.\n- [[KI_rich_default.md]]: Proportional multi-pane `Layout`, regex `Highlighter`, `RichHandler` logging, and JSON formatting.\n- [[KI_rich_live.md]]: Dynamic terminal updating (`Live`), multi-task progress meters (`Progress`), and IPython shims.\n- [[KI_rich_emoji.md]]: Emoji parsing, `Color` color models (Standard/256/Truecolor), and Windows console backends.\n- [[KI_rich_null.md]]: Internal ratio math, text wrapping routines, and Win32 low-level structures.\n- [[KI_rich_unicode11-0-0.md]] & [[KI_rich_unicode5-0-0.md]]: Unicode East Asian character width lookup tables.\n\n## Entry Points & Public API\n\n- `rich.print`: Direct drop-in replacement for `print()` with rich markup formatting.\n- `rich.inspect`: Introspective object visualizer.\n- `rich.get_console()`: Global default `Console` instance accessor.\n- `rich.traceback.install()`: Installs Rich exception handler for formatted stack traces.\n\n## Testing & Verification\n\n- Test command: `pytest tests/`\n\n## Architecture Notes\n\n- Follows the Rich Console Protocol (`__rich__` and `__rich_console__`).\n- Renders to atomic `Segment` instances before emitting ANSI escape sequences or Win32 calls.\n- Supports degradation/fallbacks for terminals without 24-bit TrueColor or Windows legacy console environments.\n\n## Related KIs\n\n- [[KI_rich_align.md]]\n- [[KI_rich_region.md]]\n- [[KI_rich_syntax.md]]\n- [[KI_rich_markdown.md]]\n- [[KI_rich_default.md]]\n- [[KI_rich_live.md]]\n- [[KI_rich_emoji.md]]\n- [[KI_rich_null.md]]\n- [[KI_rich_unicode11-0-0.md]]\n- [[KI_rich_unicode5-0-0.md]]\n"}],"details":{"server":"ki-manager","tool":"ki_read"},"isError":false,"durationMs":32,"timestamp":1794174252633},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"tool_mcp__ki_manager__ki_read_FPa63nxXzUqGl5Txe3Xu","toolName":"mcp__ki_manager__ki_read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# ADR-0002: Render Protocol & Component Isolation\n\n- **Status:** Accepted\n- **Date:** 2026-11-08\n- **Deciders:** Rich Architectural Maintainers\n\n## Context\n\nRich supports arbitrary nested UI components (such as Panels inside Tables inside Trees). If custom components were allowed to mutate shared rendering options or directly manipulate the `Console` buffer, rendering would become non-deterministic, thread-unsafe, and incompatible with real-time displays like `Live` and `Progress`.\n\n## Decision\n\n1. **Mandatory Console Protocol:**  \n   All visual components must implement the public generator protocol:\n   ```python\n   def __rich_console__(self, console: \"Console\", options: \"ConsoleOptions\") -> \"RenderResult\":\n       ...\n       yield Segment(...)\n   ```\n   A component may optionally implement `__rich_measure__(self, console: \"Console\", options: \"ConsoleOptions\") -> Measurement` for dynamic sizing.\n\n2. **Strict Component Isolation Invariants:**\n   - **No Buffer Access:** Components must NEVER access or write to `console._buffer` or `console.file` directly. All output must be returned via `yield` as an iterable of `Segment` or renderable objects.\n   - **Options Immutability:** The passed `options: ConsoleOptions` instance is strictly read-only. Components must never mutate its fields. To adjust constraints for child components, use `options.update(...)` which returns a fresh copy.\n   - **Stateless Yielding:** Generators must be re-entrant and idempotent so that multiple render passes (e.g. measuring then rendering) produce identical results without side effects.\n\n3. **Internal Spacing Convention for Inline Badges:**\n   - In accordance with repository design conventions, inline badge components must enclose their inner text with exactly one space of padding inside the boundary caps: `\"( \"` + content + `\" )\"` for pill badges, and `\"[\" + \" \"` + content + `\" ]\"` for square badges.\n   - Example: `Badge(\"DEPLOYED\", pill=True, icon=\"★\")` must yield segments rendering as `\"( ★ DEPLOYED )\"`. Square badges render as `\"[ SYSTEM ALERT ]\"`. Measurement must include the 4 cells occupied by borders and inner spaces.\n\n## Consequences\n\n- Components can be composed arbitrarily without side effects.\n- Direct console buffer writes or mutating shared options is treated as an architectural violation and rejected in code review.\n- Ensures seamless integration with `Live` displays and virtual screen buffers.\n"}],"details":{"server":"ki-manager","tool":"ki_read"},"isError":false,"durationMs":44,"timestamp":1794174252636},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"tool_mcp__ki_manager__ki_read_uhx8UJ6Q0Gs1Bn5mu9H3","toolName":"mcp__ki_manager__ki_read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# ADR-0003: Style Composition & ANSI Sequences\n\n- **Status:** Accepted\n- **Date:** 2026-11-08\n- **Deciders:** Rich Architectural Maintainers\n\n## Context\n\nStyling in terminals requires combining foreground colors, background colors, links, and various text attributes (bold, italic, underline, reverse, etc.). Rich needs an immutable, high-performance styling algebra that supports cascading inheritance, markup parsing, and export to both ANSI terminals and web formats (HTML/SVG).\n\n## Decision\n\n1. **Immutable Style Class:**  \n   The `Style` object is immutable and hashable with internal caching:\n   - Attributes (bold, underline, double_underline, italic, blink, etc.) use tri-state values (`True`, `False`, `None` where `None` indicates inherit/unset).\n2. **Style Composition Algebra (`+` operator):**  \n   Style addition (`style1 + style2`) cascades attributes from left to right:\n   - Attributes defined in `style2` override attributes in `style1` if set (`is not None`).\n   - Unset attributes (`None`) in `style2` inherit values from `style1`.\n3. **ANSI Sequence Mapping & Exporters:**  \n   Every new style modifier must maintain synchronization across:\n   - Terminal ANSI code generator: open code (e.g. `\\x1b[4:2m` or `\\x1b[21m`) and reset/close code.\n   - Default style definitions (`rich/default_styles.py`).\n   - Markup parser (`rich/markup.py`) to recognize `[modifier]...[/]`.\n   - Exporters (`rich/terminal_theme.py`, `rich/_export_format.py`) for SVG and HTML rendering.\n\n## Consequences\n\n- Full consistency between CLI console output, HTML export, and SVG snapshots.\n- Guarantees predictable cascading style resolution across nested tags.\n"}],"details":{"server":"ki-manager","tool":"ki_read"},"isError":false,"durationMs":56,"timestamp":1794174252646}]}
